{
  "$comment": "Rules of the tiered pre-merge E2E gate (scripts/e2e-gate.mjs, .claude/hooks/e2e-before-merge.sh, #355, #446). No glob or label selects the whole suite: `E2E_GATE=full` in the hook's environment (the coordinator's merge of shared-infrastructure PRs) and an unresolved or truncated file list do; `npm run release` runs it itself. A changed file adds the specs of every `map` rule whose `paths` match it (names are basenames of tests/e2e/*.spec.ts); the first group of rules covers the risk areas of .claude/issue-workflow.md (their `area` says what the specs exercise), the later ones the page and component areas. A change in tests/e2e/helpers/** adds the specs that import the helper, directly or through another helper, read from the imports at gate time. A changed i18n value or `data-testid` adds every spec whose text (or an imported helper's) contains it, whatever file the change sits in (#525: the old value of a changed or removed key, the sibling values of an added or removed key, the static prefix of a dynamic testid; `byText` in the decision). A PR touching a `design.paths` file also runs `design.specs` (the rendered Impeccable scan and the /ui style fingerprint, #66), in the style tier too, which then becomes `targeted` (reason `style-only + design scan`). The final set is `smoke` + design + mapped + touched specs + label/testid matches + the `E2E-specs:` line of the PR body. A changed file that matches nothing runs `smoke` only and is reported as `unmapped` (so is a changed helper that no spec imports; unit-test files, their helpers and fixtures are exempt), and tests/scripts/e2e-gate.test.ts fails when a file of components/, composables/, lib/, pages/, utils/, plugins/, layouts/ or types/ maps to no spec beyond `smoke` and is not on its short allow-list. The gate's own files (this file, .claude/hooks/e2e-*.sh, .claude/hooks/e2e-*.pl, scripts/e2e-gate.mjs) are never docs-only. A PR whose every file is a .css file, a .vue change inside <style> blocks or comments, docs or tests/e2e/snapshots/** runs no E2E (tier `style`; only its changed specs run if it touches tests/e2e/*.spec.ts). In fast testing mode, which drops the `design` specs, the `catalog` rule keeps the style fingerprint (kd#230): a changed file under `catalog.paths` (assets/css, app.config.ts) or a `.vue` file under `catalog.components` whose component has a `catalog/<category>/<Name>.catalog.ts` entry adds `catalog.specs`, style-only PRs included (reason `style-only + style fingerprint`), because a token or component style change moves the recorded computed styles and only the full run on main would otherwise show it.",
  "smoke": [
    "smoke",
    "drag-and-drop",
    "task-detail",
    "notion-stub-sync",
    "data-safety",
    "completion-undo",
    "source-failure"
  ],
  "design": {
    "area": "rendered Impeccable detector matrix (surfaces x 1280/390) and ARIA snapshots of the empty, loading and error states: run for every PR touching a UI path, style-only ones included (CSS can hide what the screen reader gets)",
    "paths": [
      "components/**",
      "pages/**",
      "layouts/**",
      "assets/**",
      "app.vue",
      "app.config.ts",
      "lib/icons.ts",
      "i18n/locales/**"
    ],
    "specs": [
      "design-detect",
      "state-structure",
      "ui-catalog"
    ]
  },
  "catalog": {
    "area": "style fingerprint of the /ui samples (#66) in fast mode: any stylesheet or theme change (not an image), and a component that has a catalog entry, can move a recorded computed style; one cheap spec (~25 s) instead of the whole design set",
    "paths": [
      "assets/css/**",
      "app.config.ts"
    ],
    "components": "components/**",
    "specs": [
      "ui-catalog"
    ]
  },
